        with gems.
  - key: empu
    title:
      id: Sang empu menempa
      en: The empu at the forge
    text:
      id: Ayo, kita hunus bilahnya! Bilah keris ditempa oleh seorang empu, perajin
        yang sangat dihormati. Beberapa jenis besi dan nikel dipanaskan di bara api,
        dipukul, lalu dilipat, puluhan hingga ratusan kali. Setelah itu, bilah direndam
        dalam warangan, campuran air jeruk nipis dan batu arsenik. Besinya menjadi
        hitam, sementara nikelnya tetap putih keperakan. Dari situlah pola pamor
        muncul.
      en: Let's draw the blade! A keris blade is forged by an empu, a highly respected
        craftsman. Several kinds of iron and nickel are heated in glowing coals,
        hammered and folded, dozens or even hundreds of times. Then the blade is
        soaked in warangan, a mix of lime juice and arsenic ore. The iron turns black
        while the nickel stays silvery white. That's how the pamor pattern appears.
    stage: 1
    focusHotspot: 
    voiceID: {fileID: 8300000, guid: decba66b3b5b53740a7b869642ec42f5, type: 3}
    voiceEN: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1cd785944cefdb64bb0d8bf720c1089c, type: 3}
    cuesID:
